By following this technical methodology, you can analyze how advanced persistent threats might bypass modern AV detection. The use of XOR-encrypted shellcode, process injection, registry modification, and persistence through WMI event subscriptions can help evade detection. Additionally, API unhooking techniques and heuristic bypass methods using fragmented code execution patterns can further evade detection. This analysis provides valuable insights for defensive purposes, helping to improve the effectiveness of AV software and other defensive measures.

